MewStage vendor patch multi-host/0003 (third_party/NOTICE): a dispatcher for a host that runs no Application. Window
and DispatcherTimer found their dispatcher only through a running Application, so under an embedded host every
deferred job was dropped: DispatcherTimer never ticked (TextBox caret blink, RepeatButton auto-repeat, ScrollViewer
idle timer, key-chord timeout, toast expiry, long press) and BeginInvoke work never ran (deferred Tab focus into
ListBox / TreeView / GridView rows, the hover re-check after a scroll). An internal Application.ThreadDispatcher (per
thread) is the fallback when no Application is running; the MewStage backend binds a ManagedUiDispatcher it pumps
once per frame to each UI thread, the way upstream's Browser and Headless hosts pump theirs. A running Application's
dispatcher still wins, so MewUI's own platform hosts behave exactly as before. Applies after multi-host/0001.

--- a/Controls/Window.cs
+++ b/Controls/Window.cs
@@ -1295,7 +1295,8 @@
     /// </summary>
     public IGraphicsFactory GraphicsFactory => Application.IsRunning ? Application.Current.GraphicsFactory : Application.DefaultGraphicsFactory;
 
-    internal IDispatcher? ApplicationDispatcher => Application.IsRunning ? Application.Current.Dispatcher : null;
+    // MewStage vendor patch multi-host/0003: falls back to the dispatcher an embedded host bound to this thread.
+    internal IDispatcher? ApplicationDispatcher => Application.ResolveDispatcher();
 
